# Auth walkthrough. Works with VS Code REST Client and JetBrains HTTP Client.
# 1. Start the stack and load the demo tenants: `make up && make seed`
# 2. List the tenants (dev mode) and put one id in http-client.env.json (`tenantId`).
# 3. Run the requests in order.

### Tenants you can log in to (AUTH_MODE=dev only; powers the frontend's tenant picker)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/dev-tenants

### Issue a dev token (AUTH_MODE=dev only)
# @name devToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/dev-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantId}}",
  "subject": "maya@forwarder.example",
  "roles": ["admin"],
  "expires_in_seconds": 3600
}

### Who am I?
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken.response.body.access_token}}

### Create an API key (secret is shown once; retries with the same key replay the response)
# @name apiKey
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: create-crm-key-001

{
  "name": "CRM sync",
  "scopes": ["events:write", "workflows:read"]
}

### Call the API with the API key
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey.response.body.secret}}

### The key lacks admin:manage -> 403 problem+json
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey.response.body.secret}}

### List API keys (cursor pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/api-keys?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken.response.body.access_token}}

### Revoke the API key
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/auth/api-keys/{{apiKey.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken.response.body.access_token}}

### The revoked key no longer authenticates -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey.response.body.secret}}
